@startuml
' NewEra POS - Design sequence diagram: UC5 Return Rental, condition, late fee and damage (Contracts 26 and 27), W11 draft
' Team D - editable source of assets/dsd_uc5_record_condition.png
' Render with: java -jar plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tpng assets/dsd_uc5_record_condition.puml
' Participants: classes of the logical view (architecture.md 4.2). Operations: system_interfaces.md 3.5, 4.1 and 4.3.
' Messages marked <<new>> are not in the logical view or in system_interfaces.md yet (sent to Borja for the design class diagram).

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam dpi 130
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #444444
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #1F4E79
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF1FB
skinparam BoxPadding 6
skinparam SequenceGroupBackgroundColor #F4F8FD
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #1F4E79
skinparam SequenceDividerBackgroundColor #EAF1FB
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #B8A04A
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam LegendBorderColor #1F4E79
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 190

title NewEra POS - Design sequence diagram: UC5 Return Rental, condition and late fee (Contracts 26-27)

box "UI layer (ui.api)" #F4F8FD
  participant ":RentalReturn\nController" as Ctl
end box
box "Application / domain layer" #F4F8FD
  participant ":RentalReturn\nHandler" as H
  participant ":Manager\nApproval" as MA
  participant "rr:\nRentalReturn" as RR
  participant "line:\nRentalLineItem" as L
end box
box "application.interfaces" #F4F8FD
  participant ":TaxCalculator" as Tax
  participant ":Settings\nRepository" as Set
  participant ":HRSystem" as HR
  participant ":EmployeeList" as EL
end box

== recordCondition(condition, damageNote) - Contract 26 ==
[-> Ctl : PUT /api/rental-returns/{id}/condition\n{"condition", "damageNote"}
Ctl -> Ctl : DAMAGED needs a damageNote (400 if empty)
Ctl -> H : recordCondition(condition, damageNote)
H -> RR : recordCondition(condition, damageNote, today) <<new>>
RR -> L : dueDate(), feePerDay(), deposit()
L --> RR : due date, rental fee per day, deposit
RR -> RR : daysLate = whole days after the due date (0 if on time)\nlateFee = daysLate x fee per day (BR-16)
RR --> H : lateFee
note right of RR
  Information Expert: the rental return has the dates,
  the fee and the deposit. The status of the Item
  is not changed here.
end note

opt daysLate > 0
  H -> Tax : calculateTax(TaxRequest: late fee line)
  note right of Tax
    Timeout 5 s in the adapter (AD-07).
  end note
  Tax --> H : TaxResult
  alt TaxResult OK
    H -> RR : setLateFeeTax(tax, false) <<new>>
  else NOT_AVAILABLE (7a1)
    H -> Set : current()
    Set --> H : Settings (default tax rate)
    H -> H : tax = lateFee x default rate
    H -> RR : setLateFeeTax(tax, true) <<new>>
    note right of RR
      true: tax to be corrected (BR-02, IR-05).
      The fallback is decided by the handler (AD-07).
    end note
  end
end

alt UNDAMAGED
  H -> RR : calculateRefund() <<new>>
  RR -> RR : refundTotal = max(0, deposit - lateFee - tax) (BR-10)\namountDue = late fee + tax - deposit, if above the deposit (7b)
  RR --> H : refundTotal, amountDue
  H --> Ctl : days late, late fee, tax, refund or amount still due
  [<-- Ctl : 200 parts of the calculation\n(taxToBeCorrected when the default rate was used)
else DAMAGED (6a)
  note over H, RR
    The late fee and its tax are only recorded, not charged (6a.4).
    The damage stays pending until confirmDamage; refundTotal is set there.
  end note
  H --> Ctl : store manager needed
  [<-- Ctl : 200 damage pending, D-01 opens
end

== confirmDamage(managerID, pin) - Contract 27 ==
[-> Ctl : POST /api/rental-returns/{id}/damage-confirmation\n{"manager"}
Ctl -> H : confirmDamage(managerID, pin)
H -> MA : check(managerID, pin)
MA -> HR : checkEmployee(managerID, pin)
note right of HR
  Timeout 5 s (IR-09).
end note
HR --> MA : EmployeeCheck
opt NOT_AVAILABLE (UC4 6c4, IR-09)
  MA -> EL : find(managerID)
  EL --> MA : Optional<EmployeeEntry>\n(PIN as a salted hash, DR-11)
  MA -> MA : entry.isActiveStoreManager()\nand entry.pinMatches(pin)
end
MA -> MA : drop the pin (NFR-08)
MA --> H : ApprovalResult(OK, manager)\nor ApprovalResult(REFUSED)
note right of MA
  The same check as in UC4 (dsd_uc4_confirmSessionReview):
  with OK, ManagerApproval gives the manager (Employee).
end note
alt ApprovalResult OK
  H -> RR : confirmDamage(manager: Employee) <<new>>
  RR -> RR : confirmedBy = manager\namountKept = deposit, refundTotal = 0, amountDue = 0 (BR-10)
  RR --> H : refundTotal = 0
  H --> Ctl : damage confirmed
  [<-- Ctl : 200 damage confirmed, refund 0
else ApprovalResult REFUSED (not a store manager or wrong PIN)
  H --> Ctl : refused
  [<-- Ctl : 403 the condition stays pending (FR-52)
end

legend bottom left
  **GRASP**
  Controller: RentalReturnController and RentalReturnHandler, as in the other UC5 diagrams.
  Information Expert: RentalReturn calculates the days late, the late fee, the refund and the amount still due; RentalLineItem gives the due date, the fee and the deposit.
  Pure Fabrication, High Cohesion: ManagerApproval checks the store manager for UC1, UC2, UC5 and the manager functions, so the check is written once.
  Protected Variations: TaxCalculator and HRSystem are interfaces; the adapter applies the timeout and the handler chooses the fallback (AD-04, AD-07).
endlegend
@enduml
